invariant: INV-33
file: webpki_pin.c
catches: webpki_session_test
reason: pins alone offer the raw key alone, the offer before
  docs/decisions.md 65, so a server that holds both types may not select
  X.509 even though the client accepts a pinned leaf, and one that selects
  it anyway is refused in EncryptedExtensions. test/webpki_pins_cases.h's
  pins-alone offer row, which wants both types, objects.

--- old
    return (uint8_t)((1U << CH_CERT_TYPE_RAW_PUBLIC_KEY) | (1U << CH_CERT_TYPE_X509));
--- new
    return (uint8_t)((1U << CH_CERT_TYPE_RAW_PUBLIC_KEY) |
                     (cfg->anchor_count > 0 ? (1U << CH_CERT_TYPE_X509) : 0U));
